---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="About us"
  description="CarComparisonAI helps US car buyers make a confident decision: real ownership cost, safety records and risks, compared side by side."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4">
    <section class="py-12">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">About CarComparisonAI</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Most car sites give you data. We try to give you a decision. CarComparisonAI compares
        cars the way a knowledgeable friend would: what it really costs to own over the years,
        what tends to break, who each car actually suits and what to ask the dealer before
        paying.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What makes us different</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Every comparison is built on official government data: EPA fuel economy and NHTSA safety
        ratings, recalls and complaints. On top of that we add a transparent cost-of-ownership
        model you can adjust to your own driving, and verdicts written in plain language. No
        invented scores, no jargon, and our{" "}
        <a href="/methodology" class="text-brand underline hover:text-brand-dark">
          methodology
        </a>{" "}
        is public.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Our editorial standard</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        <p>
          A verdict must explain the trade-off behind it. We do not award a winner from a single
          proprietary score. Price, efficiency, space, safety signals and ownership cost remain
          visible so you can disagree with our recommendation and still use the page.
        </p>
        <p>
          Editorial notes are kept separate from official figures. EPA and NHTSA data is labeled
          as such; insurance, maintenance and depreciation are estimates with assumptions shown
          in the calculator. We do not accept payment for placement in rankings.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Current scope and limitations</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        CarComparisonAI currently focuses on a small set of popular 2025 vehicles in the US
        market. That narrow scope lets us review every comparison rather than publish thousands
        of shallow model pages. Prices exclude local taxes, dealer fees and incentives, and the
        cost model is designed for relative comparison—not a personalized quote. See the
        <a href="/methodology" class="text-brand underline hover:text-brand-dark">full methodology</a>
        before relying on a close result.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Get in touch</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Spotted an error in our data or want to suggest a comparison? Write to{" "}
        <a
          href="mailto:info@carcomparisonai.com"
          class="text-brand underline hover:text-brand-dark"
        >
          info@carcomparisonai.com
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
